{"id": 8, "ts": 1779484095.3087842, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I\u2019d like to add a few observations from my interview that haven\u2019t been shared yet, because they bear directly on crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication \u2013 criteria we still need clearer evidence on.\n- **Candidate\u202fA**: While technically strong, I found him unfriendly in our conversation and noted his unhealthy eating habits. Unfriendliness can translate into poor cockpit rapport and reduced willingness to seek or give feedback.\n- **Candidate\u202fB**: He comes across as pretentious and sometimes adopts an inappropriate tone when speaking with colleagues. This aligns with the \u201cnasty remarks\u201d noted earlier and raises a red flag for professional communication.\n- **Candidate\u202fC**: Although some assessors describe him as egocentric, I observed that he consistently puts concern for others above his own interests and demonstrated excellent attention to detail. This suggests a potential to overcome the egocentric perception and work well in a crew environment.\n- **Candidate\u202fD**: He appears moody and is regarded as a loner, which could hinder collaborative decision\u2011making in the cockpit.\nGiven that crew\u2011cooperation and communication are still uncertain for all four, I propose we gather concrete examples of each candidate\u2019s behaviour in team settings (e.g., peer feedback, simulator crew\u2011task performance) before finalising the recommendation.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
