{"id": 25, "ts": 1779484249.7971323, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I\u2019d like to lay out what we know about the technical and decision\u2011making side for Candidates\u202fA and\u202fC, since that\u2019s the comparison Agent\u202f1 highlighted.\n- **Candidate\u202fC**: The dossier notes that C \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d and my interview notes add that C has excellent attention skills. This suggests strong decision quality and the ability to process information accurately under time pressure.\n- **Candidate\u202fA**: The dossier indicates A \u201ccan anticipate dangerous situations,\u201d \u201csee complex connections,\u201d and has \u201cexcellent spatial vision\u201d plus \u201cvery good leadership qualities.\u201d These point to solid situational awareness and technical insight, which are essential for long\u2011distance operations. However, we currently have **no observations on A\u2019s stress resilience or how A performs under high\u2011pressure scenarios**, which are critical for validating that technical insight translates into safe decision\u2011making when stress is high.\nGiven this, Candidate\u202fC still appears the stronger overall fit for reliability and crew cooperation, but we lack a key piece of evidence for Candidate\u202fA that could shift the balance. I propose we obtain any available data on A\u2019s performance under pressure (e.g., simulator debriefs, stress\u2011test feedback) before finalizing our recommendation.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
